For the first time ever, I have a good character (I think), LV 13, 105 HP, 
AC -13, Excalibur, DragonBane. I'm trying to figure out a lot of the things 
I read you masters talking about (until this character, I had paranoid 
suspicions that you guys were all playing a big joke on me). I've made it 
to the castle, but I don't have a musical instrument and I can't remember 
everything that was discussed about playing MasterMind.  No biggie, though. 
I'll figure it out.

My question(s) is/are:

1. How many times should you give gold to a like-aligned priest? Is one time
   sufficient, or will repeated offering give more boons by your diety? If
   my hero Jim Bakker were here, he'd say give til it hurts, but what is the
   real truth?

2. What do I need to ingest to get more strength? My character only has 12
   (using +2 ring of strength) and that isn't enough to carry a couple of
   artifacts, dragon scale mail, and all the goodies I've collected.

3. Once armor's protective value has been knocked down (from acid attacks,
   etc.) is there a way to "regain armor class" like you can regain ability?
   My blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail is now +0. Is there a way to make it
   +3 again short of "Enchant Armor"?

4. Are shopkeepers Ferengi or are they Deevils (from Deva)?

5. What was the name of that wizard who was always trying to catch Smurfs?
   What was his cats name?  'Frobozz' is getting old for a character name,
   and my cat Milo is wondering why I always curse him while I'm sitting at
   the big table with the funny box on it (especially when he keeps eating
   that tasty floating eye).

Observation: Aside from using it to buy things and giving to priests, gold
	     isn't all that important, is it? All this time, I've been a
	     disgusting capitalist, trying to amass as much gold as possible,
	     and I've got probably 60,000 GP, I've given bunches to the
	     church, and I'm can't seem to do much with it, except use up my
	     precious strength points.  Since the object is to get the AoY,
	     after I have a pick-axe, and have given some to the church, do
	     I need gold other than to raise my score in the top-10 list?

